  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-04-04T20:55:52.730Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, the behavior when the bandwidth limit is exceeded seems to be that a single UdonBehaviour can queue up an arbitrary amount of data in the transmit queue. This can take tens of seconds to flush out, in some cases. This does not seem ideal; there's not a good way to detect when this is happening and back off to reduce bandwidth usage, so this could easily result in death runs where things get further and further behind.\nI would suggest that, if a single UdonBehaviour has too many untransmitted serializations, then any RequestSerialization calls be deferred until the queue can be flushed.\nYou can reproduce the problem behaviour in this world: https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_cea2ef6d-13b3-439a-b876-539bb1691f57\nEnter 4096 in one of the text boxes to start (attempted) transmitting way faster than the bandwidth limit. Let this run for a while, then set it back to 1. You'll see that (on the receive side) the received sequence numbers are well behind _instancewide_ for quite some time.",
